            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Tags are a JUnit Platform concept for marking and filtering tests. The programming model for adding tags to containers and tests is defined by the testing framework. For example, in JUnit Jupiter based tests, the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Tag"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " annotation (see "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "writing-tests/tagging-and-filtering.html"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "writing-tests/tagging-and-filtering.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") should be used. For JUnit 4 based tests, the Vintage engine maps "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Category"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " annotations to tags (see "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Categories Support"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "migrating-from-junit4.html#categories-support"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). Other testing frameworks may define their own annotation or other means for users to specify tags."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
